%% /run-issues orchestrator — state machine
%% Source of truth for orchestrate.sh control flow. Update both together.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> S0_Idle

    S0_Idle --> S1_PickIssue: trigger (cmd or poller)
    S1_PickIssue --> S2_Lock: candidate found
    S1_PickIssue --> S0_Idle: no candidate

    S2_Lock --> S3_Claim: lock acquired
    S2_Lock --> S0_Idle: lock held by other run

    S3_Claim --> S4_Worktree: claim verified
    S3_Claim --> S2_Lock: claim race lost (retry)

    S4_Worktree --> S5_DBClone: worktree ready
    S5_DBClone --> S6_CycleReview: clone ok or not needed

    S6_CycleReview --> S7_ReviewGate: cycle-review output written
    S7_ReviewGate --> S8_Implementer: PROCEED
    S7_ReviewGate --> S11_PostRunCleanup: BLOCKER or NEEDS_CLARIFICATION

    S8_Implementer --> S9_Evolution: implementer commits done
    S9_Evolution --> S10_PR: evolution refinements done
    S10_PR --> S11_PostRunCleanup: PR opened

    S11_PostRunCleanup --> S12_Finalize: cleanup done
    S12_Finalize --> [*]

    %% Failure transitions can occur from any active state into Finalize
    S1_PickIssue --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S2_Lock --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S3_Claim --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S4_Worktree --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S5_DBClone --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S6_CycleReview --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S8_Implementer --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S9_Evolution --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
    S10_PR --> S12_Finalize: fatal error
